🌍 Top Countries Actively Hiring Indian Software Developers
🇳🇱 Netherlands
Companies: Booking.com, Adyen, ASML, ING, bunq

Visa: Highly Skilled Migrant Visa (very friendly for Indians)

Why: English-friendly, high salaries, expat benefits (30% ruling)

🇩🇪 Germany
Companies: SAP, Siemens, Zalando, Deutsche Telekom, N26

Visa: EU Blue Card or Job Seeker Visa

Why: Strong demand, especially in backend, embedded, DevOps, AI

🇮🇪 Ireland
Companies: Google, Facebook, HubSpot, Workday

Visa: Critical Skills Employment Permit

Why: Low corporate tax attracts tech giants; English-speaking

🇬🇧 United Kingdom
Companies: Revolut, Monzo, Deliveroo, HSBC Tech

Visa: Skilled Worker Visa

Why: Post-Brexit shortage of tech talent, high demand for Java, Python, ML

🇨🇦 Canada
Companies: Shopify, RBC, TD Bank, Amazon, startups

Visa: Global Talent Stream (fast 2-week processing)

Why: Strong tech immigration policies, good work-life balance

🇺🇸 United States
Companies: Google, Amazon, Meta, Microsoft, top startups

Visa: H-1B, L1, O1 — but competitive and lottery-based

Why: Still highest-paying tech jobs globally despite visa hurdles

🇦🇺 Australia
Companies: Atlassian, Canva, Commonwealth Bank

Visa: Subclass 482 (Temporary Skill Shortage Visa)

Why: Shortage of software engineers, high quality of life

🇸🇬 Singapore
Companies: Grab, Shopee, SEA, DBS, ByteDance

Visa: EP (Employment Pass)

Why: Asia’s tech hub, no language barrier, tax-friendly

🇸🇪 Sweden
Companies: Spotify, Klarna, Volvo, Ericsson

Visa: Work Permit (easy to get if offered a job)

Why: Great work-life balance, rising demand for software engineers

